{"@context":{"CIP100":"https://github.com/cardano-foundation/CIPs/blob/master/CIP-0100/README.md#","hashAlgorithm":"CIP100:hashAlgorithm","body":{"@id":"CIP100:body","@context":{"references":{"@id":"CIP100:references","@container":"@set","@context":{"GovernanceMetadata":"CIP100:GovernanceMetadataReference","Other":"CIP100:OtherReference","label":"CIP100:reference-label","uri":"CIP100:reference-uri","referenceHash":{"@id":"CIP100:referenceHash","@context":{"hashDigest":"CIP100:hashDigest","hashAlgorithm":"CIP100:hashAlgorithm"}}}},"comment":"CIP100:comment","externalUpdates":{"@id":"CIP100:externalUpdates","@context":{"title":"CIP100:update-title","uri":"CIP100:uri"}}}},"authors":{"@id":"CIP100:authors","@container":"@set","@context":{"name":"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name","witness":{"@id":"CIP100:witness","@context":{"witnessAlgorithm":"CIP100:witnessAlgorithm","publicKey":"CIP100:publicKey","signature":"CIP100:signature"}}}}},"authors":[],"body":{"comment":"Technically, although Christina came second after Cardano Curia in the preliminary vote, this does not mean that she would have taken first place if Cardano Curia had not been present. In reality, it is unknown how the votes would have been redistributed in that case (for example, those who voted for Cardano Curia might not have voted for Christina, in which case she still would not have come first).\n\nHowever, as I have said many times before, I aim to reduce bureaucracy in Cardano, and I generally believe that most of these preliminary votes make little sense and only add confusion, especially since the final vote still has to pass a certain threshold anyway. Therefore, it is completely irrelevant to me what happened in the preliminary vote (or whether it happened at all), as I believe that in the final vote everyone ultimately expresses their own opinion.\n\nSince I believe that adding an 8th member to the Constitutional Committee would be beneficial, and that Christina is a suitable candidate for this 8th member, I vote Yes."},"hashAlgorithm":"blake2b-256"}